<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Elan in Dainippon epilepsy drug deal.</title>
<headline>Elan in Dainippon epilepsy drug deal.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish pharmaceuticals group Elan Corporation Plc said on Tuesday it had signed a licensing and distribution agreement with Dainippon Pharmaceutical Co Ltd for the Japanese group's anti-epileptic drug Zonisamide.</p>
<p>Elan said it would receive exclusive sales and marketing rights for the drug throughout North America. It will market Zonisamide in the U.S. through its unit Athena Neurosciences Inc. Financial terms of the agreement were not disclosed.</p>
<p>The company said epilepsy affected an estimated two million people in the U.S..</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
